WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.134 --> 00:00:16.036
arrived at the shore of Kidd's Creek where the Jolly Roger was anchored.

2
00:00:17.337 --> 00:00:19.218
He had quickly crawled across the island.

3
00:00:20.518 --> 00:00:24.401
After seeing the silent crocodile, Peter had decided to imitate it.

4
00:00:26.042 --> 00:00:32.072
In fact, he tick-tocked so perfectly the way the creature had done that the other animals let him

5
00:00:32.152 --> 00:00:33.253
pass unharmed.

6
00:00:34.433 --> 00:00:41.095
The crocodile, which had become fond of the sound, followed him, hoping to get his tick-tock back.

7
00:00:41.115 --> 00:00:44.716
"This time, it's Hook or me!"

8
00:00:45.596 --> 00:00:48.737
Peter vowed to himself, then dived into the water.

9
00:00:49.817 --> 00:00:53.918
He had been tick-tocking so long that he hardly thought about it anymore.

10
00:00:55.199 --> 00:01:00.140
He swam to the ship and climbed up the side—tick-tocking all the while.

11
00:01:01.964 --> 00:01:05.485
When the boys looked over the side, he signaled them to be quiet.

12
00:01:06.526 --> 00:01:09.447
Then he climbed around the hull to the other side of the ship.

13
00:01:10.648 --> 00:01:15.730
He peeked over the rail and saw the boys in chains and Wendy tied to the mast.

14
00:01:16.730 --> 00:01:20.612
They all saw him too, and he gave them another signal to be quiet.

15
00:01:21.692 --> 00:01:23.733
Hook was trembling on the deck.

16
00:01:23.753 --> 00:01:26.414
"How clever of me!"

17
00:01:27.154 --> 00:01:28.615
Peter thought, grinning.

18
00:01:29.635 --> 00:01:31.276
At the back of the deck was the cabin.

19
00:01:32.204 --> 00:01:33.745
Peter watched the cabin door.

20
00:01:34.866 --> 00:01:38.369
When one of the pirates came out, Peter stabbed him with his dagger.

21
00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:42.172
He covered the pirate's mouth to muffle his dying moan.

22
00:01:43.894 --> 00:01:46.896
The boys watched as Peter threw the pirate overboard.

23
00:01:47.857 --> 00:01:50.699
There was a loud splash, followed by silence.

24
00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:54.562
Then Peter vanished into the cabin.

25
00:01:54.583 --> 00:01:56.884
"Pirate number one!"

26
00:01:57.505 --> 00:01:58.286
whispered Slightly.

27
00:01:59.346 --> 00:02:03.173
The pirates had heard a big splash, and then the tick-tocking had stopped.

28
00:02:04.513 --> 00:02:07.334
All they could hear now was the sound of their breathing.

29
00:02:07.354 --> 00:02:13.057
"It's gone, Captain," Smee said, wiping his spectacles.

30
00:02:13.077 --> 00:02:15.158
"All is still again."

31
00:02:16.318 --> 00:02:18.999
Listening hard, Hook slowly raised his head.

32
00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:26.082
Hearing nothing, he got up and yelled, "Get those boys on the plank!"

33
00:02:26.102 --> 00:02:27.302
His nerve was back.

34
00:02:29.123 --> 00:02:33.036
But the boys had seen him act like a coward, and it made him hate them more.

35
00:02:33.056 --> 00:02:35.737
"Fetch my whip from the cabin!"

36
00:02:36.337 --> 00:02:37.838
he yelled to one of his pirates.

37
00:02:37.858 --> 00:02:39.658
"The cabin!

38
00:02:40.078 --> 00:02:41.099
Peter's in there!"

39
00:02:41.739 --> 00:02:43.919
thought the children, as they looked at each other.

40
00:02:43.939 --> 00:02:50.661
"Ay, ay," said Bill Jukes, cheerfully opening the cabin door.

41
00:02:52.042 --> 00:02:56.683
As soon as the door closed behind him, a terrible scream was heard from inside.

42
00:02:57.603 --> 00:02:59.944
It was followed by a sound like a rooster crowing.

43
00:03:01.216 --> 00:03:04.418
The boys knew the sound, but the pirates looked puzzled.

44
00:03:04.438 --> 00:03:06.500
"Number two!"

45
00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:09.402
Slightly said quietly to the boys.

46
00:03:09.422 --> 00:03:11.343
"What was that?"

47
00:03:11.983 --> 00:03:12.704
shouted Hook.

48
00:03:13.764 --> 00:03:16.947
Cecco thought for a moment, and then ran into the cabin.

49
00:03:18.407 --> 00:03:20.149
Shocked, he stumbled out.

50
00:03:20.169 --> 00:03:23.651
"What's the matter?"

51
00:03:24.291 --> 00:03:24.992
Hook yelled.

52
00:03:25.012 --> 00:03:28.994
"Juke's been stabbed to death," cried Cecco.

53
00:03:29.014 --> 00:03:33.121
"The cabin is dark, and there is some terrible thing in there.

54
00:03:33.321 --> 00:03:34.481
It's crowing."

55
00:03:34.501 --> 00:03:39.283
"Cecco," Hook ordered, "go find out what that thing is!"

56
00:03:39.303 --> 00:03:42.345
"No, no!

57
00:03:42.805 --> 00:03:43.945
I can't do that!"

58
00:03:44.745 --> 00:03:46.506
Cecco said, desperately.

59
00:03:47.707 --> 00:03:49.367
Hook lifted his iron claw.

60
00:03:49.387 --> 00:03:52.209
"Are you disobeying me?"

61
00:03:52.889 --> 00:03:53.449
he yelled.

62
00:03:54.529 --> 00:03:58.771
Trembling, Cecco followed Hook's order and went slowly into the cabin.

63
00:03:59.972 --> 00:04:04.691
Again, they all heard a deadly scream followed by a crowing sound.

64
00:04:04.711 --> 00:04:06.672
"Number three!"

65
00:04:07.392 --> 00:04:08.293
Slightly called out.

66
00:04:09.254 --> 00:04:10.534
Hook yelled at his crew.

67
00:04:10.555 --> 00:04:12.896
"Who will get this crowing thing?"

68
00:04:13.897 --> 00:04:17.639
"Wait until Cecco comes out," cried Starkey.

69
00:04:18.740 --> 00:04:20.181
The other pirates agreed.

70
00:04:20.201 --> 00:04:22.663
"Yes, let's wait!"

71
00:04:22.683 --> 00:04:26.645
"Did I hear you volunteer, Starkey?"

72
00:04:27.286 --> 00:04:27.866
said Hook.

73
00:04:29.127 --> 00:04:30.428
"No, by thunder!"

74
00:04:31.104 --> 00:04:32.025
growled Starkey.

75
00:04:32.045 --> 00:04:35.067
"I'll hang before I go in there."

76
00:04:35.087 --> 00:04:37.970
"Is this mutiny?"

77
00:04:38.650 --> 00:04:40.592
asked Hook, lifting his claw.

78
00:04:40.612 --> 00:04:43.975
"Captain, please, have mercy!"

79
00:04:44.635 --> 00:04:46.117
the fearful pirate begged.

80
00:04:48.699 --> 00:04:53.623
Starkey backed away, and Hook strode toward him, his hook ready to strike.

81
00:04:55.024 --> 00:04:59.708
Starkey looked around for help, but all the other pirates were looking down at their feet.

82
00:05:00.832 --> 00:05:05.462
With a hopeless scream, Starkey leapt off the ship and into the sea.

83
00:05:05.482 --> 00:05:07.386
"Number four!"

84
00:05:08.008 --> 00:05:09.611
called Slightly, happily.
